From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:42:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: aop: Find the boot arguments in version 4
 firmware headers

The AOP firmware's main image starts with an RTKit header: the magic
"uuid", a version and, among other fields, the offset and size of the
boot argument block that the loader fills in. The driver reads them at
0x48, where the iPadOS 16 and 17 images (header version 5) keep them.

iOS 15's images, such as the A9 iPhones' aopfw-s8000aop (19H422 and
15.8.8), use header version 4, which lacks two words before the boot
argument fields and keeps them at 0x40; the iOS 15 kernel accepts only
that version. In aop-s8000.bin the words at 0x48 and 0x4c are zero, so
the driver finds an empty block, fails with "unexpected boot arguments in
apple/aop-s8000.bin: -2" and never starts the AOP: without this change
the iPhones' enabled AOP cannot come up at all. With it, the block at
0x4f3a8 (0x19a bytes, STKG first) is patched and an iPhone 6s Plus
reports AOP IS READY with its accelerometer, gyroscope and barometer.

Take the version 4 location when the header says so, and keep the
version 5 location for every other image, as before: the iPads' AOP
images keep working whatever their header version.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #219, commit 390e338c; only version 4 selects
 the new location, and images without the magic or with another version
 keep the version 5 location instead of being refused, so no board whose
 AOP starts today can lose it]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
index 5c23317d1..7990ddb9b 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
@@ -54,9 +54,17 @@
 
 #define APPLE_AOP_CONTROL_AUTO_BOOT	0x0
 
-/* Main image header: location of the boot argument key/value block */
-#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_OFFSET	0x48
-#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_SIZE	0x4c
+/*
+ * Main image: an RTKit header ("uuid", then its version) that gives the
+ * offset and size of the boot argument key/value block. Version 5 (iPadOS 16)
+ * has two more words before them than version 4 (iOS 15).
+ */
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_MAGIC		0x20
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_MAGIC_UUID	0x64697575	/* "uuid" */
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_VERSION		0x24
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_V4	0x40
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_V5	0x48
+#define APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_HEADER_SIZE	0x50
 
 #define APPLE_AOP_FOURCC(a, b, c, d)                                     \
 	(((u32)(a) << 24) | ((u32)(b) << 16) | ((u32)(c) << 8) | (u32)(d))
@@ -281,11 +289,17 @@ static void apple_aop_add_bootarg(struct apple_aop_bootarg *args, unsigned int *
 static int apple_aop_patch_bootargs(struct apple_aop *aop, u8 *image, size_t size,
 				    struct apple_aop_bootarg *args, unsigned int count)
 {
-	size_t offset, end, pos;
+	size_t offset, end, pos, location;
 	unsigned int i;
 
-	offset = get_unaligned_le32(image + APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_OFFSET);
-	end = get_unaligned_le32(image + APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_SIZE);
+	if (get_unaligned_le32(image + APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_MAGIC) == APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_MAGIC_UUID &&
+	    get_unaligned_le32(image + APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_VERSION) == 4)
+		location = APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_V4;
+	else
+		location = APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_V5;
+
+	offset = get_unaligned_le32(image + location);
+	end = get_unaligned_le32(image + location + 4);
 	if (offset >= size || end > size - offset)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	end += offset;
@@ -373,7 +394,7 @@ static int apple_aop_load(struct apple_aop *aop, u64 ecid)
 		goto out_main;
 
 	if (main_fw->size > aop->sram_size || main_fw->size % 4 ||
-	    main_fw->size < APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_BOOTARGS_SIZE + 4 || !ext_fw->size) {
+	    main_fw->size < APPLE_AOP_IMAGE_HEADER_SIZE || !ext_fw->size) {
 		dev_err(aop->dev, "invalid firmware sizes %zu/%zu\n",
 			main_fw->size, ext_fw->size);
 		ret = -EINVAL;
